  "claim": "A Shoulder-fired missile is a rocket propelled weapon, sometimes referred to as the \"Stovepipe\". Colonel Leslie Alfred Skinner helped develop the weapon in 1976.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Leslie Skinner. Sentence: He played a leading role in the development of several rocket propelled weapons during World War II, notably the first shoulder-fired missile system, the Bazooka.\nPage: Bazooka. Sentence: Also referred to as the \"Stovepipe\", the innovative bazooka was among the first generation of rocket-propelled anti-tank weapons used in infantry combat.\nPage: Shoulder-fired missile. Sentence: In many instances, although not technically defining all shoulder-fired missiles, the name Bazooka is used as an informal name regularly, although the actual Bazooka is a type of original shoulder-fired missile in its own right.",
